# Keep the Docker build context to what the image needs.
.git
.github
.venv
node_modules
.next
.cache
.difflens
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
site
dist
docs
specs
skills
vdd
tests
tests-webapp
output
design
data/*
# The published benchmark records are imported statically into the build, so exactly this one file has
# to reach the build context. `data` alone would exclude it and Docker cannot re-include a file whose
# parent directory is excluded — measured both ways: with `data`, `COPY data/benchmarks.json` fails
# with "excluded by .dockerignore".
!data/benchmarks.json
.npmrc
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
.DS_Store
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The library reference is built into the web image (Dockerfile.web, docs stage), so the docs
# sources and their assets must survive the ignore list above — later rules win.
!docs
!docs/**

# Bytecode from a working tree must not enter the image: the whole point of Dockerfile.api is that
# the engine in the image is the engine at the built commit, and a stale .pyc is a file from neither.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
